# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 1: one act read two ways

== cheered at one place, frowned on at the other
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
calls: WR
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: community, friends
horizon: months
roles: regular, keeper, go-between
who: go-between
cast_want: caught
earth: two of your places pull apart over the step you took lately: one cheers it, the other frowns, and both want you to answer for it
times: People whose circles disagree about them tend to hold back, take part less and decide later (cross-pressures: Lazarsfeld 1944; Mutz 2002)
gap: 3-8
scene: Word of the step {N} took lately has gone round both places. At {place_b} people clap {N} on the back and call it the bravest thing in years; at {place_a} the talk stops when {N} walks in, and someone says it is not how things are done. A friend who goes to both says each one is waiting to hear {N} answer for it.
scene W: {N} made the choice in good faith, and owes both places one straight account of it, not two stories.
scene U: The act is the same in both places, so the difference must lie in the places. {N} wants to know what each is really reacting to.
scene B: Both names count for something. {N} weighs which one is worth more to keep, and what losing the other would cost.
scene R: The cheers at {place_b} felt wonderful, and the cold looks at {place_a} sting more than {N} expected.
scene G: {N} has belonged to {place_a} a long time, and {place_b} feels like home in another way. Neither is easy to give up.
- W | keep away from both for a season, so neither place splits over it | caught: back | v: conformity, benevolence | chance: 80
- U | stand with {place_a}: hear their reasons out, and grant where they are right | caught: side_a | v: self-direction, universalism | chance: 85
- B | stand with {place_b}, where the step has made a name worth keeping | caught: side_b | v: achievement, power | chance: 60
- R | bring two old hands from {place_a} along to {place_b} one night, to see why | caught: bridge | v: stimulation, benevolence | chance: 50
- G | keep each place as it always was, and never bring one up at the other | caught: apart | v: tradition, security | chance: 75
- W>U | stand with {place_b} on principle, and give {place_a} a full, fair account of why | caught: side_b | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 60
- U>B | work out who counts at each place, and broker a sit-down that saves everyone's face | caught: bridge | v: achievement, power | chance: 55
- B>R | keep each place in the dark about the other, and enjoy the cheers while they last | caught: apart | v: hedonism, security | chance: 80
- R>G | drop both on a whim, and spend the season's evenings back with the family | caught: back | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 90
- G>W | stand with {place_a}, the older tie, and own that the step let it down | caught: side_a | v: tradition, conformity | mark: owned up | chance: 65
works: Within a season the talk dies down, and one of the places is warmer to {N} than before.
works: Someone at the other place says, unasked, that they have come to see the step differently.
fails: One place cools for good: the greetings there grow shorter, and the invitations stop.
fails: Both places feel let down, and for a while {N} is half a stranger in each.

