- W>B | call a fair sit-down between the two places, on terms that protect {Ns} own standing | caught: bridge | v: security, power | chance: 60
- U>R | plan the weeks so the two crowds never meet, and keep the nights at {place_b} free | caught: apart | v: hedonism, self-direction | chance: 75
- B>G | stop going to both for a season, and put the hours into home and kin | caught: back | v: security, tradition | chance: 85
- R>W | stand with {place_a} at once, and tell {place_b} to its face the choice was right | caught: side_a | v: conformity, stimulation | chance: 55
- G>U | stay loyal to the friends at {place_b}, and ask them what they saw | caught: side_b | v: benevolence, self-direction | chance: 62
works: Each place hears {N} out, and in time both accept the choice was made in good faith.
works: One place warms to {N} more than ever, and the other quietly lets the matter drop.
fails: {place_b} cools: the calls stop, and {N} hears about the good nights only afterwards.
fails: Both places feel {N} chose the other, and the welcome in each turns merely polite.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 2: two places ask opposite things in one season

== one place calls for calm, the other for a stand
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
calls: WR
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: community, friends
horizon: months
roles: keeper, regular, neighbour
who: go-between
cast_want: caught
earth: two of your places ask opposite things this season: one wants you to stand up and be counted, the other to keep the peace
times: People caught between circles that disagree on a public dispute often stay out of it, though they also come to understand the other side better (cross-pressures: Mutz 2002)
gap: 3-8
scene: A dispute has stirred up the neighbourhood this season, and both of {Ns} places have taken a side. {place_b} is getting ready to make itself heard and wants {N} out front with them on the night. At {place_a} the word is to keep calm and stay out of it, and the people there are counting on {N} to be seen keeping the peace.
scene W: Order matters, and so does a wrong put right. {N} feels both pulls as a duty.
scene U: {N} wants to know what the stand is really for, and what keeping calm would really achieve.
scene B: Whoever ends up on the winning side will remember who stood with them. {N} weighs the odds.
scene R: {N} can already feel the night at {place_b}: the noise, the heat, the sense of being part of something.
scene G: {place_a} has kept the peace here for generations. That still counts for something.
- W | stand with {place_b}, because a wrong left unanswered is still a wrong | caught: side_b | v: universalism, benevolence | chance: 65
- U | draft a joint statement both places could sign, and carry it between them | caught: bridge | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 55
- B | tell each place privately what it wants to hear, and keep them from comparing notes | caught: apart | v: security, power | chance: 82
- R | skip the night and the meetings alike, and go off somewhere free for a while | caught: back | v: hedonism, self-direction | chance: 80
- G | stand with {place_a}, which has kept the peace here longer than anyone | caught: side_a | v: tradition, security | chance: 80
- W>R | keep firm, separate rules: free nights at {place_b}, calm at {place_a}, and no crossover | caught: apart | v: conformity, self-direction | chance: 75
- U>G | think it through slowly at home, and let the season pass with the family | caught: back | v: tradition, security | chance: 85
- B>W | stand with {place_a}, and take a visible role keeping order on the night | caught: side_a | v: power, conformity | chance: 58
- R>U | throw in with {place_b}, and stay up nights getting the facts straight for them | caught: side_b | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 60
- G>B | bring the elders of both places to one table, and come away the one they trust | caught: bridge | v: tradition, power | chance: 60
works: The night passes without trouble, and one place thanks {N} openly for the part they played.
works: The two places find a little common ground, and both mention {N} when they tell the story.
fails: The place {N} did not stand with takes it hard, and the welcome there cools for a long while.
fails: Neither place is satisfied, and both quietly stop asking {N} for anything.

== two places claim the same evenings
