gap: 3-8
scene: It is the busy season at both of {Ns} places at once. {place_a} has drawn up its rota and counts on {N} for three evenings a week until it ends. {place_b} has its own big run of nights coming, the ones everyone will talk about for a year, and the regulars take it for granted that {N} will be there. There are not enough evenings for both.
scene W: {N} gave {place_a} a word when the rota went round. A promise is a promise, but so is friendship.
scene U: {N} counts the evenings and the weeks. There may be a way to fit both in, or there may not.
scene B: {N} asks which place will matter more in a year, and which favour is likelier to be repaid.
scene R: The run at {place_b} is the kind of thing that happens once. {N} aches to be there every night.
scene G: {place_a} has asked the same of every member for as long as anyone remembers. That is how it holds together.
- W | sit both sides down, agree a fair split of the evenings, and keep to it | caught: bridge | v: conformity, benevolence | chance: 50
- U | plan the weeks to the hour, and keep each place's calendar out of the other's sight | caught: apart | v: self-direction, achievement | chance: 78
- B | skip both for the season, and put the evenings into a side business | caught: back | v: achievement, power | chance: 85
- R | stand with {place_a}, because the thought of letting those people down is unbearable | caught: side_a | v: benevolence | chance: 80
- G | stand with {place_b}, where the old friends are, and be there every night | caught: side_b | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 68
- W>G | step back from both, and keep the season's evenings for the family, as promised long ago | caught: back | v: tradition, conformity | mark: kept your word | chance: 90
- U>W | stand with {place_a}, once the numbers show the rota falls apart otherwise | caught: side_a | v: security, conformity | chance: 62
- B>U | stand with {place_b}, and get backstage to learn how such nights are run | caught: side_b | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 55
- R>B | throw one big night for both crowds on the spot, and be the toast of it | caught: bridge | v: stimulation, power | chance: 60
- G>R | keep the old habits at {place_a} and the free nights at {place_b} in separate weeks | caught: apart | v: tradition, hedonism | chance: 72
works: Both places get enough of {N} to be content, and someone at each says they could not have managed without them.
works: One place warms to {N} for the season, and the other lets it go without a grudge.
fails: The place that went short remembers, and asks less of {N} the next time round.
fails: Both places feel shortchanged, and {N} ends the season tired and a little alone.

# Chroma library, modern Earth: CAUGHT BETWEEN TWO PLACES, part 3 (S3 Their places' eyes, v22.3, cast_want: caught DRAFT).
# Enemy pair UR: {place_a} is a reasons-and-study place (a reading circle, an evening class, a lab or design office, a
# debating society, a library group); {place_b} a feeling-and-freedom place (a band, a late-night crowd, a protest
# group, a dance hall, a street football side). The Engine fills both names and the go-between (who: go-between).
#   pair 1 (one act read two ways)          1a UR, cross s1: a bold step, cheered at {place_b}, doubted at {place_a}
#                                           1b WBG, cross s2: a careful choice, praised at {place_a}, scorned at {place_b}
#   pair 2 (opposite asks in one season)    2a UR, cross s3: {place_a} wants the evenings for work, {place_b} for its big nights
#                                           2b WBG, cross s4: {place_b} wants a public stand, {place_a} asks for calm
# Every option carries caught: side_a | side_b | bridge | apart | back; per lead letter, the one-letter option plus its own cross sum to chance 140.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 1: one act read two ways

== a bold step cheered at one place, doubted at another
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
calls: UR
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: community, friends
horizon: months
roles: regular, go-between, friend
who: go-between
cast_want: caught
earth: two of your places pull apart over a bold step you took lately: one cheers your nerve, the other asks whether you thought it through
times: People whose circles judge the same act differently tend to hold back and feel torn, and groups do judge one act by different standards (cross-pressures: Lazarsfeld 1944, Mutz 2002; Graham, Haidt and Nosek 2009)
gap: 3-8
scene: Word of the step {N} took lately has got around. At {place_b} they clap {N} on the back for it: it took nerve, and it came from the heart. At {place_a} the talk is quieter and cooler, about haste and things not weighed. A friend who goes to both says each place is waiting to hear {N} answer for it.
scene W: {N} owes each place an honest hearing, and owes neither a fight on the other's ground.
scene U: Both readings make some sense, and {N} wants to understand why one step looks so different from each side.
scene B: Cheered in one place and doubted in the other is a position too, and {N} weighs which good name is worth more.
scene R: {N} did it because it felt right, and the cool looks at {place_a} sting more than they should.
scene G: These are both {Ns} people now, and a home with two rooms does not wall one of them off.
- W | keep a firm rule: what is said at each place stays at that place | caught: apart | v: conformity, security | chance: 80
- U | stay away from both for a few weeks, and think the step through again | caught: back | v: self-direction | chance: 85
- B | side with {place_a}, call it a lesson learned, and keep the name that opens doors | caught: side_a | v: achievement, power | chance: 85
- R | stand up at {place_b} and say it again, louder, whatever {place_a} thinks | caught: side_b | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: made an enemy | chance: 62
- G | invite the oldest hands of both places to one table, like neighbours of old | caught: bridge | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 50
- W>U | own up at {place_a} that the step was rushed, and ask help thinking it through | caught: side_a | v: conformity, self-direction | mark: owned up | chance: 60
- U>B | side with {place_b}: make the case for the step, and take the credit there | caught: side_b | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 55
- B>R | call in favours to get both places into one room, and let them mix | caught: bridge | v: power, stimulation | chance: 55
- R>G | give heart and soul to each place on its own night, never bringing one along | caught: apart | v: stimulation, benevolence | chance: 78
- G>W | let the season pass quietly, trusting both places to settle as they always do | caught: back | v: tradition, security | chance: 90
works: {place_b} keeps a warm spot for {N}, and at {place_a} the doubt fades into a shrug by spring.
works: In the end both places hear the whole story, and {N} is welcome in each, a little more known than before.
fails: {place_a} goes cool, and the seat {N} had there is quietly given to someone else.
fails: Both places feel {N} held something back, and the welcome in each runs thinner for a season.

== a careful choice praised at one place, scorned at another
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
calls: WBG
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: community, friends
horizon: months
roles: regular, go-between, friend
who: go-between
cast_want: caught
earth: two of your places pull apart over a careful choice you made lately: one calls it sound, the other calls it cold, even a letdown
times: Belonging to circles that cross makes a person both torn and a natural go-between, and people meet clashing demands by choosing, keeping roles apart or stepping back (cross-pressures: Lazarsfeld 1944, Mutz 2002; role strain: Goode 1960)
gap: 3-8
scene: The choice {N} made lately was the careful one, and {place_a} approves: weighed, reasoned, sound. At {place_b} it reads otherwise, as playing it safe and letting the others down when it counted. A friend who goes to both carries the talk both ways and says both places want to hear {N} answer for it.
scene W: Somebody has been treated unfairly in all this talk, and {N} will not add to it by taking cheap sides.
scene U: {N} can set out every reason for the choice, and still wonders whether the reasons are the whole story.
scene B: {N} made the choice for good reasons of their own, and neither place gets to decide what it was worth.
scene R: The word letdown hurts, because the people at {place_b} are the ones {N} feels most alive with.
scene G: {N} has belonged to both places for a while now, and old ties do not have to break over one choice.
- W | stay away from both for a month, rather than sit as judge between friends | caught: back | v: conformity, benevolence | chance: 85
- U | stand with {place_a}, and set out the reasons for the choice plainly | caught: side_a | v: self-direction, universalism | chance: 82
- B | side with {place_b}: its crowd is bigger, and its good word travels further | caught: side_b | v: power, achievement | chance: 62
- R | bring friends from {place_b} along to {place_a} one evening, and let them meet face to face | caught: bridge | v: stimulation, benevolence | chance: 50
- G | keep each place in its own part of the week, the way it has always been | caught: apart | v: tradition, security | chance: 82
- W>B | side with {place_b}: make a proper apology there, and earn back a good name | caught: side_b | v: conformity, achievement | mark: owned up | chance: 55
- U>R | plan an open evening for both places, where everyone can say how it felt | caught: bridge | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 58
- B>G | play it carefully: give each place the version it likes, and keep both seats | caught: apart | v: security, tradition | chance: 78
- R>W | take a break from both, before tempers say things nobody can take back | caught: back | v: benevolence, security | chance: 90
- G>U | stand with {place_a} quietly and patiently, and let time show the choice was sound | caught: side_a | v: tradition, universalism | chance: 58
works: {place_a} counts {N} among its steadiest, and by summer {place_b} has stopped teasing and started asking why.
works: The two places end up hearing each other out, and {N} is the one both now trust to carry word.
fails: {place_b} closes ranks, and its next nights go ahead without {N}.
fails: Both places sense {N} saying different things to each, and the welcome cools on both sides.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 2: two places ask opposite things in one season

== the season of hard work and the season of big nights
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
calls: UR
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: friends, community
horizon: months
roles: regular, go-between, colleague
who: go-between
cast_want: caught
earth: two of your places pull apart over one season: one wants your evenings for its hardest stretch of work, the other for its biggest nights
times: People pulled between clashing groups often take part less and put off deciding, and handle the strain by choosing one, splitting their time or stepping back (cross-pressures: Lazarsfeld 1944, Mutz 2002; role strain: Goode 1960)
gap: 3-8
scene: The same season, two calls on the same evenings. {place_a} has its hardest stretch of the year ahead and is counting on {N} every week, prepared and present. {place_b} has its run of big nights, the ones people talk about for years, and wants {N} there for every one. A friend who goes to both hears both sides grumble and asks {N} which it is going to be.
scene W: {N} gave their word to {place_a} before the season began, and a promise does not bend for a good night out.
scene U: {N} counts the weeks and the hours, sure there is a sensible way to fit both if it is planned well.
scene B: One place will remember who carried the work, the other who showed up on the big nights, and {N} weighs which memory pays.
scene R: Nights like the ones at {place_b} do not come twice, and {N} can already feel them slipping past.
scene G: Seasons like this come and go; what lasts is the people {N} goes home to at the end of them.
- W | keep the promise made to {place_a}, and give it every evening this season | caught: side_a | v: conformity, achievement | mark: kept your word | chance: 85
- U | side with {place_b}, having reckoned that the work can wait and these nights cannot | caught: side_b | v: self-direction, stimulation | chance: 60
- B | get both places into one room for a night, as the one who made it happen | caught: bridge | v: power, achievement | chance: 52
- R | go wherever the heart pulls each evening, and never speak of one place at the other | caught: apart | v: stimulation, hedonism | chance: 72
- G | step back from both and spend the season at home among family | caught: back | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 86
- W>R | get both places to agree a fair split of evenings, and keep free nights free | caught: bridge | v: universalism, hedonism | chance: 55
- U>G | plan the weeks so each place gets its nights, and neither hears about the other | caught: apart | v: security, tradition | chance: 80
- B>W | plead a full diary to both for a month, and spare everyone the quarrel | caught: back | v: security, conformity | chance: 88
- R>U | throw everything into the push at {place_a} this season, heart and soul | caught: side_a | v: achievement, stimulation | chance: 68
- G>B | stand by {place_b} out of loyalty, and become a face it cannot do without | caught: side_b | v: tradition, achievement | chance: 54
works: One place gets the season it hoped for from {N}, and the other, a little to its own surprise, understands.
works: By the season's end both places count on {N}, and nobody remembers which evenings went where.
fails: {place_b} stops saving {N} a place, and the big nights go on without them.
fails: Both places feel short-changed, and {N} ends the season tired and only half welcome in each.

== the call to stand up and the call to keep calm
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
calls: WBG
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: community, friends
horizon: months
roles: regular, go-between, neighbour
who: go-between
cast_want: caught
earth: two of your places pull apart in one season: one wants you to stand up and be counted, the other asks you to keep the peace
times: When a person's circles disagree, many go quiet and take part less, though they also come to see the other side's reasons more clearly (cross-pressures: Lazarsfeld 1944, Mutz 2002)
gap: 3-8
scene: Something has stirred {place_b} to anger, an unfairness close to its heart, and it wants every one of its people to stand up and be counted, loudly and in public. At {place_a} the word is the opposite: wait for the facts, keep its name out of it, say nothing in heat. {N} belongs to both, and both have noticed. A friend who goes to both says the next few weeks will show where {N} stands.
scene W: If a wrong is being done, someone has to say so, but {N} also knows that a fair hearing comes before a verdict.
scene U: {N} wants the facts first: who did what, and whether the anger at {place_b} has the whole picture.
scene B: A public stand makes a name and makes enemies, and {N} weighs which of those this season can afford.
scene R: The anger at {place_b} is {Ns} anger too, and keeping calm feels like swallowing something hot.
scene G: Quarrels like this blow through every few years, and the places people love are still standing afterwards.
- W | stand up with {place_b} in public, because the wrong done to them is a real wrong | caught: side_b | v: universalism, benevolence | mark: made an enemy | chance: 58
- U | bring the facts to both places, and arrange a meeting where each hears the other | caught: bridge | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 55
- B | keep both: turn up quietly for {place_b}, and stay out of it at {place_a} | caught: apart | v: security, power | chance: 80
- R | walk away from both for a while: the fighting has taken the joy out of each | caught: back | v: hedonism, self-direction | chance: 80
- G | keep the peace with {place_a}: hot words fade, and the places people love remain | caught: side_a | v: tradition, security | chance: 85
- W>G | keep to proper form: speak up only at {place_b}, and never carry it into {place_a} | caught: apart | v: conformity, tradition | chance: 82
- U>W | hold back from both until the facts are in, so nobody is wronged in haste | caught: back | v: universalism, security | chance: 85
- B>U | side with {place_a}, and use its standing to get the matter properly looked into | caught: side_a | v: power, universalism | chance: 60
- R>B | stand with {place_b} out front, where everyone can see {N} took a stand | caught: side_b | v: self-direction, stimulation | chance: 60
- G>R | gather both places around one long table, so the anger can be spoken face to face | caught: bridge | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 55
works: The season's anger cools, and the place {N} stood by remembers it, warmly, for a long time.
works: A bridge holds: the two places end the season on speaking terms, and {N} is trusted in both.
fails: The place {N} did not stand with cools for good, and the old greetings there turn polite and short.
fails: Both places read {N} as half-hearted, and neither saves a seat for them in the weeks that follow.

