cast_want: caught
earth: the step you took lately is still talked about, and now both of your places want you to answer for it: one wants you to speak up for it, the other wants you to take it back
times: People caught between two roles usually cope by choosing one, keeping the two apart or stepping back from both (role strain: Goode 1960)
gap: 3-8
scene: A friend who goes to both brings the word to each side. {place_a} would like {N} to stand up at its next meeting and explain the choice {N} made, as an example for others. {place_b} would like {N} to say, plainly and in front of the old faces, that it was a mistake. Neither request is unkind. They cannot both be granted.
scene W: Both places asked fairly and in good faith. {N} owes each a straight answer, whatever the cost.
scene U: {N} wants time to think it through: what was really decided, and what each place is actually asking for.
scene B: Whichever room {N} answers first, {N} is choosing whose good opinion counts. Better to choose with care.
scene R: Being asked to perform the choice, or to disown it, makes {N} want to say something sharp to both.
scene G: Home is the place that knew {N} first. That has to mean something when the old faces ask.
