- U | step back from both for a season, and think the step through before answering anyone | caught: back | v: self-direction | chance: 85
- B | stand with {place_a}, where the step has made a name worth keeping | caught: side_a | v: achievement, power | chance: 90
- R | stand with {place_b} on impulse, and say sorry for the hurt, not the choice | caught: side_b | v: benevolence, stimulation | mark: owned up | chance: 65
- G | ask the eldest at {place_b} to sit down with the people of {place_a}, over tea | caught: bridge | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 50
- W>B | answer {place_a} formally, by its rules, and take the place it holds open | caught: side_a | v: achievement, conformity | chance: 60
- U>R | think it through, then stand with {place_b}, where it simply feels right to be | caught: side_b | v: self-direction, hedonism | chance: 55
- B>G | call in favours on both sides to set up one shared evening that suits everyone | caught: bridge | v: power, benevolence | chance: 50
- R>W | tell each place warmly what it needs to hear, so no one there gets hurt | caught: apart | v: benevolence | chance: 75
- G>U | go back to the family for a while, and let time show what the step meant | caught: back | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 90
works: The answer lands well, and the place that asked for it draws {N} closer than before.
works: The two places find, through {N}, that they were less far apart than the talk made out, and {N} is trusted in both.
fails: The other place takes the answer as a slight, and {N} is quietly left off its lists for the season.
fails: Neither place is satisfied, and both start to speak of {N} as someone who cannot be pinned down.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 2: two places ask opposite things in one season

== one place wants a stand, the other wants peace
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
calls: UG
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: community, place
horizon: months
roles: keeper, regular, neighbour
who: go-between
cast_want: caught
earth: in the same season one of your places wants you to stand up and be counted for a change, and the other asks you to keep the peace and leave things be
times: People whose networks disagree on a public question tend to decide later and take part less, though they understand the other side better (cross-pressures: Lazarsfeld 1944; Mutz 2002)
gap: 3-8
scene: {place_a} has drawn up a plan to change how something in the neighbourhood is done, and it wants names on it, {Ns} among the first. At {place_b} the same plan is spoken of as a slight on everything the old families built, and {N} is asked, kindly but firmly, to keep out of it. The open meeting is in a month. Everyone will see where {N} sits.
scene W: A person with ties on both sides has a duty not to tear the neighbourhood in two, whatever they privately think.
scene U: {N} has read the plan and it is sound, mostly. The parts that worry {place_b} could be fixed.
scene B: Whoever wins this, the winners will remember who stood with them. {N} would like to be on the winning side.
scene R: {N} is tired of being careful. Someone should just stand up and say what everyone is thinking, on both sides.
scene G: The old families have kept this place what it is. Change will come, but not like this, not at their expense.
- W | step back from both until the meeting is done, as fairness to each side requires | caught: back | v: conformity, universalism | chance: 80
- U | stand with {place_a} and be counted, with the figures to show why | caught: side_a | v: self-direction, universalism | chance: 85
- B | stand with {place_b}, where the long memories and the real sway sit | caught: side_b | v: power, security | chance: 60
- R | stand up at the open meeting and speak for both sides, from the heart, unplanned | caught: bridge | v: stimulation, benevolence | chance: 50
- G | keep {place_b} out of {place_a}'s business, as the old families always have | caught: apart | v: tradition, security | chance: 75
- W>R | honour the call for peace from {place_b} as a duty, and win back easy evenings | caught: side_b | v: conformity, hedonism | mark: kept your word | chance: 60
- U>G | draft a version of the plan that keeps what {place_b} holds dear, and show both | caught: bridge | v: universalism, tradition | chance: 55
- B>W | back the plan quietly and keep the peace loudly: each place hears only its part | caught: apart | v: security, conformity | chance: 80
- R>U | drop both for a few weeks on a whim, and go see how others did it | caught: back | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 90
- G>B | stand with {place_a}, and use every old family tie to win the vote | caught: side_a | v: tradition, power | mark: made an enemy | chance: 65
works: The meeting goes {Ns} way, and the place {N} stood with treats {N} as one of its own.
works: The plan is changed enough that both places can live with it, and people on both sides credit {N} for it.
fails: The place {N} did not stand with closes ranks, and greetings there turn short and formal.
fails: The meeting turns bitter, and both places blame {N} for not doing more to stop it.

