works: The season ends well where {N} gave the time, and the people there say they could not have done it without {N}.
works: Both places come through the season, and the old hands at {place_b} even drop by to see what {place_a} has built.
fails: The place that went without {N} manages, but someone there says {N} has changed, and it gets around.
fails: Stretched between the two, {N} lets both down in small ways, and by the end neither place quite counts on {N}.

# Chroma library, modern Earth: CAUGHT BETWEEN TWO PLACES (S3 Their places' eyes, v22.3; agent 5, enemy pair BG).
# Two of the character's places pull opposite ways. The Engine fills {place_a} with the B-led place (ambition and
# advantage: a business club, a fast-growing firm, a traders' association, a developers' circle) and {place_b} with the
# G-led place (roots and tradition: the old congregation, a village hall, a family trade, an allotment society, the
# elders' table, a nature group). cast_want: caught; every option carries caught: side_a | side_b | bridge | apart | back.
#   pair 1 one act read two ways          1a BG (s1) / 1b WUR (s2)
#   pair 2 opposite asks in one season    2a BG (s3) / 2b WUR (s4)
# Chances: each colour's one-colour option plus its cross option (first letter) sum to 140 in every moment.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 1: one act read two ways

== toasted at one place, frowned on at the other
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
calls: BG
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: community, friends
horizon: months
roles: regular, go-between, friend
who: go-between
cast_want: caught
earth: two of your places pull apart over something you did lately: one toasts it, the other frowns, and both want you to answer for it
times: People whose circles judge the same act differently feel pulled both ways and tend to put off taking a side (cross-pressures: Lazarsfeld 1944; Mutz 2002)
gap: 3-8
scene: Word of what {N} did lately has got round. At {place_a} people clap {N} on the shoulder and call it the bold step they always knew was coming. At {place_b} the greetings are a shade cooler, and someone says quietly that it is not how things are done there. Now both want {N} to speak to it, {place_a} at its next gathering and {place_b} face to face.
scene W: {N} wants to be fair to both: each place deserves an honest account, and the ways {place_b} keeps were there long before {N}.
scene U: Two places are reading one act by two yardsticks. {N} wants to understand both before saying a word.
scene B: The praise at {place_a} is worth something real: contacts, doors, a name. The chill at {place_b} costs less, for now.
scene R: {N} took the step because it felt right, and it stings that anyone wants it explained.
scene G: {place_b} has known {N} the longest. Its frown lands harder than any toast.
- W | stand with {place_b}, own that the step strayed from its ways, and keep them from now | caught: side_b | v: conformity, tradition | mark: owned up | chance: 60
- U | ask both places to sit down together and hear the reasons behind the step | caught: bridge | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 50
- B | enjoy the toasts at {place_a}, and say nothing of them at {place_b} | caught: apart | v: achievement, security | chance: 80
- R | leave both to their talk, and spend a few weeks somewhere that feels lighter | caught: back | v: hedonism, self-direction | chance: 85
- G | stand with {place_a}, loyal to the friends there who backed the step from the start | caught: side_a | v: benevolence, security | chance: 80
- W>U | make it a firm rule to carry no talk between the two while thinking it through | caught: apart | v: conformity, self-direction | chance: 80
- U>B | step back from both for a season, and plan the next move while the talk cools | caught: back | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 90
- B>R | stand with {place_a}, and use the backing there to go further, free of old frowns | caught: side_a | v: stimulation, achievement | chance: 60
- R>G | stand with {place_b}: go there that very evening and say, from the heart, it is home | caught: side_b | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 55
- G>W | bring the two together patiently, the old way, so neither place feels wronged | caught: bridge | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 60
works: {place_b} softens in time, and {place_a} says it thinks all the more of {N} for how it was handled.
works: The talk dies down, and by the next season both places greet {N} warmly again.
fails: One of the two places cools on {N}, and the welcome there is never quite the same.
fails: Both places feel let down, and {N} goes to each a little less often.

== the story of the step, bent in the telling
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
calls: WUR
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: community, friends
horizon: months
roles: regular, go-between, friend
who: go-between
cast_want: caught
earth: the story of something you did has travelled between two of your places and bent on the way, and each now wants to know where you stand
times: Talk carries an act from one circle to the next and changes it in the telling, and people caught between circles that disagree feel the strain of both roles (role strain: Goode 1960; cross-pressures: Mutz 2002)
gap: 3-8
scene: The tale of what {N} did has travelled between {place_a} and {place_b}, and bent on the way. At {place_b} they hear that {N} is being held up at {place_a} as proof that the old ways hold people back. At {place_a} they hear that {place_b} is making {N} pay for it. Each place now wants to hear from {N} where {N} stands.
scene W: It is not fair to anyone: neither place has the true story, and both deserve it.
scene U: {N} can trace how the tale bent at each telling, and wants it put straight before anyone decides anything.
scene B: Whichever telling wins will decide what {Ns} name is worth, at both places.
scene R: It makes {N} furious to hear the step turned into a weapon by people who were not even there.
scene G: Talk like this has split places before. {N} knows the hurt outlasts the quarrel.
- W | call both places to one meeting and give everyone the same honest account | caught: bridge | v: conformity, universalism | chance: 55
- U | keep the two separate on purpose, and tell each only what bears on it | caught: apart | v: self-direction, security | chance: 80
- B | stay away from both until it is clear which way the talk will settle | caught: back | v: security, power | chance: 90
- R | stand with {place_a} openly, where the step was cheered, and let the frowns fall | caught: side_a | v: self-direction, stimulation | chance: 80
- G | stand with {place_b}, the place that has known you longest, and let the rest go | caught: side_b | v: tradition, security | act: stand with {place_b}, the place that has known them longest, and let the rest go | chance: 65
- W>B | excuse yourself from both for the season, on the rule that private choices stay private | caught: back | v: security, conformity | act: excuse themself from both for the season, on the rule that private choices stay private | chance: 85
- U>R | stand with {place_a}, and lay out calmly why the step freed you to live your way | caught: side_a | v: self-direction | act: stand with {place_a}, and lay out calmly why the step freed them to live their way | chance: 60
- B>G | stand with {place_b}, and back its next appeal to win your welcome back | caught: side_b | v: security, tradition | act: stand with {place_b}, and back its next appeal to win their welcome back | chance: 50
- R>W | bring people from both to the same table that night, and have it out honestly | caught: bridge | v: benevolence, universalism | chance: 60
- G>U | keep each place out of the other's business, and wait quietly to see what it meant | caught: apart | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 75
works: The true story gets out at last, and someone at each place tells {N} they are glad to have heard it.
works: The tale stops bending, and {N} ends up the one both places ask when they want to know what the other thinks.
fails: The bent version sticks at one place, and {N} feels it in every greeting there.
fails: Both places decide {N} has not been straight with them, and the talk turns colder on each side.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 2: two places ask opposite things in one season

== one place wants a name on the list, the other wants quiet
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
calls: BG
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: community, friends
horizon: months
roles: regular, go-between, neighbour
who: go-between
cast_want: caught
earth: in the same season one of your places wants you to stand up and be counted for a change in the neighbourhood, and another asks you to keep out of it and keep the peace
times: People asked by two of their circles to act in opposite ways tend to delay, waver and take part less (cross-pressures: Lazarsfeld 1944; Mutz 2002)
gap: 3-8
scene: This season {place_a} is pushing hard for a change in the neighbourhood, and it wants {Ns} name on the list of supporters, said out loud. At {place_b} most people are quietly against the change, and they ask only one thing of {N}: keep out of it, and keep the peace. Both requests come in the same week, and both are put kindly.
scene W: Two fair claims pull at {N}: a cause that wants honest support, and a place that asks for peace.
scene U: {N} wants to know what the change would actually do before signing anything, or refusing to.
scene B: The list at {place_a} will be read by people who matter. A name on it, or missing from it, will be remembered.
scene R: {N} can feel which way the heart leans, and hates being asked to hush it.
scene G: The neighbourhood has seen changes come and go. {place_b} has outlasted them all.
- W | honour each place's rules within its own walls, and carry nothing between them | caught: apart | v: conformity, security | chance: 80
- U | step back from both until the facts of the change are clear | caught: back | v: self-direction, security | chance: 85
- B | stand with {place_a}, and put your name high on the list, where the right people look | caught: side_a | v: achievement, power | act: stand with {place_a}, and put their name high on the list, where the right people look | chance: 85
- R | stand with {place_b} on gut feeling, and say so with feeling | caught: side_b | v: benevolence, self-direction | chance: 65
- G | bring the oldest hands of both places together for a quiet talk, the old way | caught: bridge | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 50
- W>R | stand with {place_a} and sign, since everyone has the right to speak up | caught: side_a | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 60
- U>G | stand with {place_b}, after looking hard at what the change would cost the neighbourhood | caught: side_b | v: tradition, universalism | chance: 55
- B>W | broker a deal: a gentler plan from one side, quiet acceptance from the other | caught: bridge | v: power, universalism | chance: 55
- R>U | throw yourself into hearing out both sides, and keep what each says to yourself | caught: apart | v: stimulation, self-direction | act: throw themself into hearing out both sides, and keep what each says to themself | chance: 75
- G>B | wait it out, let the season pass, and keep your standing in both intact | caught: back | v: security, tradition | act: wait it out, let the season pass, and keep their standing in both intact | chance: 90
works: The season passes, and both places say afterwards that {N} handled it with grace.
works: The two places find a way to live with the outcome, and each counts {N} as one of its own.
fails: One place takes {Ns} answer as a slight, and asks less of {N} from then on.
fails: Both places feel {N} let them down, and the welcome cools on each side.

== one place wants the hours, the other the old ties
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-85
calls: WUR
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: community, friends
horizon: months
roles: regular, go-between, colleague
who: go-between
cast_want: caught
earth: in the same season one of your places wants your evenings for a big push, and another is counting on your loyalty in a hard stretch of its own
times: Juggling the demands of several groups at once is an ordinary strain, and people handle it by choosing one, keeping them apart or stepping back (role strain: Goode 1960)
gap: 3-8
scene: {place_a} is in the busiest stretch of its year, and it wants {N} there most evenings: the push could make a real difference for everyone in at the start. {place_b} has a hard season of its own, short of hands and long on old commitments, and it is counting on {N} the way it always has. There are not enough evenings for both.
scene W: {N} gave {place_b} a promise long ago, and gave {place_a} one more lately. Both are owed.
scene U: {N} counts the evenings, the hours and the tasks, and looks for a plan that wastes none of them.
scene B: The push at {place_a} could change where {N} stands a year from now. {place_b} will still be there afterwards.
scene R: {N} is torn between the buzz of the push and the warmth of the old crowd, and wants both tonight.
scene G: {place_b} has carried {N} through hard seasons before. Now it is the one in need.
- W | tell both places honestly you cannot do either justice this season, and step back | caught: back | v: conformity, universalism | act: tell both places honestly they cannot do either justice this season, and step back | chance: 85
- U | stand with {place_a} this season, after weighing what each evening there would build | caught: side_a | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 80
- B | stand with {place_b}, where being the one who came through will count for years | caught: side_b | v: security, achievement | chance: 60
- R | throw one big evening that brings both crowds together, and see what sparks | caught: bridge | v: stimulation, benevolence | chance: 50
- G | keep the old place and the new in separate corners of life, as always | caught: apart | v: tradition, security | chance: 70
- W>G | stand with {place_b}, and keep the promise made there long before the other | caught: side_b | v: tradition, conformity | mark: kept your word | chance: 55
- U>W | draw up a fair rota between the two places, and get both to agree to it | caught: bridge | v: universalism, conformity | chance: 60
- B>U | split the evenings shrewdly, learn what each can teach, and keep the two diaries apart | caught: apart | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 80
- R>B | drop both on a whim for a few weeks, and take the evenings for yourself | caught: back | v: hedonism, self-direction | act: drop both on a whim for a few weeks, and take the evenings for themself | chance: 90
- G>R | stand with {place_a} this season, giving it the steady loyalty that makes the push a joy | caught: side_a | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 70
works: The season ends well, and the place that got {Ns} evenings says it will not forget it.
works: Both places come through the stretch, and each is glad, in the end, of what {N} could give.
fails: The place that was left short cools on {N}, and says so to anyone who asks.
fails: Spread thin, {N} disappoints both, and is asked to less at each.
